The VoxelGI story's cue groups
==============================

What the storyboard (`storyboard.lam`) says again and again, said once: the package `godot_voxelgi_story`, which
the storyboard imports (`$$[Import* godot_voxelgi_story]`; tools/video/build.py gives it to the reader).

$[Import* std]$[Import* content]$[Import* present]$[Import* render_lab]$[Import* godot_voxelgi]

A beat's opening keys: its demonstration and panel, the callout and the insets cleared, and how far the camera
drifts while it holds; `more` are the beat's own.

$[# {opening demo panel drift more} {append {' demo {callout ""} {inset ""} panel {cameraDrift drift}} more}]

The diffuse cones the screen pass traces per pixel (gi.glsl's `voxel_gi_compute`): four at Low quality, six at
High. Chapter 8 says them and shows them (`conesShown`); its other numbers are the package's code's
(`godot_voxelgi_natives`, cost.rs).

$[# lowCones 4]
$[# highCones 6]
